## [ Normalize & Extract Alert ] → [ AI SOC Analysis ]

### 🇷🇺 Русский

Этот блок подготавливает Wazuh alert к AI-анализу.

### `Normalize & Extract Alert`

JavaScript node извлекает основные данные из входящего Wazuh alert:

- уровень события;
- Rule ID;
- описание правила;
- hostname / имя агента;
- IP-адрес агента;
- source IP;
- пользователей;
- команду;
- группы правила;
- location / log source;
- timestamp.

Значения нормализуются, чтобы отсутствующие поля не приводили к ошибкам во время дальнейшей обработки.

Node также определяет, является ли событие критическим:

`level >= criticalLevel`

### Infrastructure Context

Перед отправкой события в AI можно добавить описание вашей инфраструктуры.

Контекст может содержать:

- назначение серверов;
- важные сервисы;
- нормальные административные операции;
- особенности сетевой инфраструктуры;
- VPN / proxy;
- ожидаемые способы аутентификации;
- другие особенности вашей среды.

Чем точнее описана инфраструктура, тем полезнее AI-анализ.

**Не добавляйте в этот блок:**

- API keys;
- passwords;
- Telegram tokens;
- private credentials;
- другие secrets.

### AI Request

После извлечения данных node формирует единый JSON request для AI-модели.

Запрос содержит:

- выбранную AI model;
- system prompt;
- Wazuh alert;
- infrastructure context;
- формат ожидаемого JSON-ответа.

Следующий node `AI SOC Analysis` отправляет этот request в OpenRouter.

---













### 🇬🇧 English

This block prepares the Wazuh alert for AI analysis.

### `Normalize & Extract Alert`

The JavaScript node extracts the main fields from the incoming Wazuh alert:

- event level;
- Rule ID;
- rule description;
- hostname / agent name;
- agent IP address;
- source IP;
- users;
- command;
- rule groups;
- log location;
- timestamp.

Missing values are normalized so that incomplete Wazuh events do not break the following processing steps.

The node also determines whether the event is considered critical:

`level >= criticalLevel`

### Infrastructure Context

Before sending the event to the AI model, you can provide additional context about your infrastructure.

The context may include:

- server roles;
- important services;
- normal administrative activity;
- network architecture;
- VPN / proxy usage;
- expected authentication patterns;
- other environment-specific information.

The more accurate the infrastructure context, the more useful the AI analysis can be.

**Do not add:**

- API keys;
- passwords;
- Telegram tokens;
- private credentials;
- other secrets.

### AI Request

After extracting and normalizing the alert, the node builds a single JSON request for the AI model.

The request contains:

- the selected AI model;
- the system prompt;
- the Wazuh alert;
- infrastructure context;
- the expected JSON response schema.

The next node, `AI SOC Analysis`, sends this request to OpenRouter.

parameters.jsCode:
const item = $input.first().json;
const alert = $('Wazuh Alert Webhook').first().json.body;

// ============================================================
// Core Wazuh alert fields
// ============================================================

const level = parseInt(alert?.rule?.level ?? 0, 10);
const description = alert?.rule?.description ?? 'Unknown rule';

const agentName = alert?.agent?.name ?? 'unknown';
const agentIp = alert?.agent?.ip ?? 'N/A';

const srcIp = alert?.data?.srcip ?? null;
const dstUser = alert?.data?.dstuser ?? null;
const srcUser = alert?.data?.srcuser ?? null;
const command = alert?.data?.command ?? null;

const groups = Array.isArray(alert?.rule?.groups)
  ? alert.rule.groups.join(', ')
  : (alert?.rule?.groups ?? 'N/A');

const ruleId = alert?.rule?.id ?? 'N/A';
const location = alert?.location ?? 'N/A';


// ============================================================
// Timestamp
// ============================================================

const rawTs = alert?.timestamp ?? new Date().toISOString();

const tz = item.timezone ?? 'UTC';

const ts = new Date(rawTs).toLocaleString('en-US', {
  timeZone: tz,
  hour12: false,
});


// ============================================================
// Severity classification
// ============================================================

const criticalLevel = Number(item.criticalLevel ?? 12);

const isCritical = level >= criticalLevel;


// ============================================================
// CUSTOMIZE ME
// Infrastructure context
//
// Replace this example with information about YOUR environment.
// Do not include passwords, API keys, tokens, or other secrets.
//
// The more specific the context, the more useful the AI analysis
// can become.
//
// Example topics:
// - server roles
// - important services
// - normal authentication patterns
// - network architecture
// - VPN / proxy usage
// - expected administrative activity
// - monitoring configuration
// ============================================================

const infraContext = `
Infrastructure context:

Replace this section with a description of your environment.

Example:
- Linux servers monitored by Wazuh
- Internal authentication services
- Web and database servers
- VPN used for administrative access
- n8n used for security automation
- Active response disabled; monitoring and notification only

Do not include secrets or sensitive credentials in this section.
`;


// ============================================================
// AI prompts
// ============================================================

const systemPrompt = `
You are an AI security analyst reviewing a Wazuh SIEM alert.

Analyze the alert using the available event data and the provided
infrastructure context.

Do not invent facts that are not present in the alert or context.

${infraContext}

Return ONLY a valid JSON object.

Required schema:

{
  "risk_level": "critical|high|medium|low|unknown",
  "likely_cause": "string",
  "is_likely_false_positive": true,
  "fp_reason": "string",
  "recommended_action": ["string"],
  "investigate_commands": ["string"]
}

Rules:

1. Write human-readable explanations in Russian.
2. Keep risk_level within the allowed values.
3. likely_cause must briefly explain the most likely cause.
4. fp_reason must explain why the event may be a false positive.
5. recommended_action must contain concrete investigation or response steps.
6. investigate_commands must contain real Linux/Wazuh commands when appropriate.
7. Do not invent facts.
8. Consider hostname, IP address, username, rule ID, severity,
   command, authentication details and other available fields.
9. Do not classify an event as a false positive only because it
   appears to be a normal administrative operation.
10. If there is not enough information, use a cautious risk level
    and explain the uncertainty.
11. Do not return Markdown.
12. Do not wrap the JSON in code fences.
13. Return JSON only.
`;

const userPrompt = `
Analyze this Wazuh alert.

Host: ${agentName} (${agentIp})
Rule ID: ${ruleId}
Level: ${level}
Description: ${description}
Groups: ${groups}
Source IP: ${srcIp ?? 'N/A'}
Destination User: ${dstUser ?? 'N/A'}
Source User: ${srcUser ?? 'N/A'}
Command: ${command ?? 'N/A'}
Location: ${location}
Timestamp: ${ts}

Full Wazuh alert JSON:

${JSON.stringify(alert, null, 2)}
`;


// ============================================================
// AI request body
// ============================================================

const aiBodyObj = {
  model: item.aiModel ?? 'nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free',
  max_tokens: 1600,
  temperature: 0.2,
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'system',
      content: systemPrompt,
    },
    {
      role: 'user',
      content: userPrompt,
    },
  ],
};


// ============================================================
// Output
// ============================================================

return [
  {
    json: {
      // Configuration
      minAlertLevel: item.minAlertLevel,
      criticalLevel,
      timezone: item.timezone,
      aiModel: item.AiModel,

      // Alert fields
      level,
      description,
      agentName,
      agentIp,
      srcIp,
      dstUser,
      srcUser,
      command,
      groups,
      ruleId,
      location,
      ts,
      isCritical,

      // Prepared AI request
      aiBodyObj,
    },
  },
];

const llmResponse = $input.first().json;
const alert = $('Normalize & Extract Alert').item.json;

// Получаем ответ модели
const rawText =
  llmResponse.content?.[0]?.text ??
  llmResponse.choices?.[0]?.message?.content ??
  llmResponse.message?.content ??
  '{}';

// Парсим JSON от LLM
let analysis = {};

try {
  let cleaned = rawText
    .replace(/^```json\s*/i, '')
    .replace(/^```\s*/i, '')
    .replace(/\s*```$/i, '')
    .trim();

  analysis = JSON.parse(cleaned);
} catch (e) {
  analysis = {
    risk_level: 'unknown',
    likely_cause: 'AI-анализ не удалось разобрать.',
    is_likely_false_positive: false,
    fp_reason: '',
    recommended_action: [],
    investigate_commands: []
  };
}

// Безопасный HTML
function esc(value) {
  return String(value ?? '')
    .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
    .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
    .replace(/>/g, '&gt;');
}

const level = alert.level ?? 0;
const risk = String(analysis.risk_level ?? 'unknown').toLowerCase();

const riskEmoji = {
  critical: '🔴',
  high: '🟠',
  medium: '🟡',
  low: '🟢',
  unknown: '⚪'
}[risk] ?? '⚪';

const riskLabel = {
  critical: 'КРИТИЧЕСКИЙ',
  high: 'ВЫСОКИЙ',
  medium: 'СРЕДНИЙ',
  low: 'НИЗКИЙ',
  unknown: 'НЕИЗВЕСТНО'
}[risk] ?? 'НЕИЗВЕСТНО';

const lines = [];

lines.push(`🚨 <b>Анализ события Wazuh</b>`);
lines.push('');

lines.push(`<b>Уровень Wazuh:</b> ${esc(level)}`);
lines.push(`<b>Риск:</b> ${riskEmoji} ${riskLabel}`);
lines.push('');

lines.push(`🖥 <b>Хост:</b> ${esc(alert.agentName)}`);
lines.push(`📍 <b>IP хоста:</b> ${esc(alert.agentIp)}`);
lines.push(`🌐 <b>IP источника:</b> ${esc(alert.srcIp ?? 'неизвестно')}`);
lines.push(`📋 <b>Rule ID:</b> ${esc(alert.ruleId)}`);
lines.push(`📝 <b>Событие:</b> ${esc(alert.description)}`);
lines.push(`🕒 <b>Время:</b> ${esc(alert.ts)}`);
lines.push('');

lines.push(`🔎 <b>Предполагаемая причина:</b>`);
lines.push(esc(analysis.likely_cause ?? 'Нет данных'));
lines.push('');

lines.push(
  `⚠️ <b>Ложное срабатывание:</b> ${
    analysis.is_likely_false_positive ? 'Да' : 'Нет — требует внимания'
  }`
);

if (analysis.fp_reason) {
  lines.push('');
  lines.push(`💡 <b>Почему:</b>`);
  lines.push(esc(analysis.fp_reason));
}

if (
  Array.isArray(analysis.recommended_action) &&
  analysis.recommended_action.length
) {
  lines.push('');
  lines.push(`🛠 <b>Рекомендуемые действия:</b>`);

  analysis.recommended_action.forEach((action, index) => {
    lines.push(`${index + 1}. ${esc(action)}`);
  });
}

if (
  Array.isArray(analysis.investigate_commands) &&
  analysis.investigate_commands.length
) {
  lines.push('');
  lines.push(`🔧 <b>Команды для расследования:</b>`);
  lines.push('<pre>');

  analysis.investigate_commands.forEach((cmd, index) => {
    lines.push(`${index + 1}. ${esc(cmd)}`);
  });

  lines.push('</pre>');
}

const telegramMessage = lines.join('\n');

return [
  {
    json: {
      telegramMessage,
      level: alert.level,
      description: alert.description,
      agentName: alert.agentName,
      agentIp: alert.agentIp,
      srcIp: alert.srcIp,
      ruleId: alert.ruleId,
      riskLevel: analysis.risk_level
    }
  }
];
